X4. Spot-Check of G's 2024–2026 Literature Items

All 11 arXiv identifiers cited by G were spot-checked via web search and verified to exist with matching authors, titles, and mathematical content: arXiv:2610.28338 (Zhang-Xuan, mk! circuits), 2609.08005 (Brakensiek et al., capacity RS), 2609.05870 (Jeronimo, capacity RS), 2509.17699 (Mulder-Sterner-van Woerden, smooth twins), 2410.16355 (Tesoro et al., tensor-network Schnorr), 2510.19390 (Al-Hasso & von der Leyen, p-bit CVP), 2411.16632 (Sanchez Cano et al., VQE Schnorr), 2409.08784 (Huang et al., double index calculus), 2610.06733 (Van Kirk-Gidney, streaming Regev), 2409.03486 (Murru-Salvatori, SQUFOF/CFRAC), and 2504.21168 (Friedlander, base-sum). Two minor date/detail flags on non-arXiv-numbered mentions: Lido's provable quasi-polynomial small-char DLP paper originated in 2022 (arXiv:2206.10327, published later in FFA), and McGuire-Robinson's published TNFS lattice-sieving paper is 3D (J. Math. Cryptol., with 4D orthotope extensions in follow-up implementations).

