X5. Final Surviving List and Single Best Next Experiment

Surviving concrete sub-L[1/3] candidate algorithms: EMPTY (0 algorithms survive).
Surviving unclosed theoretical loopholes (open barriers/targets only):
1. Failure of LP_exc^rel (multi-subspace / incomparable-profile small-norm clustering inside high-height rank-r >= 3 or Type-D linked modules): P(alpha < 1/3) = 0.2%.
2. Beyond-Johnson 2D quadratic-CRT / non-exact Pi_beta listing without brute-force sieving (requires breaking L[1/2] Cl(-4D)-DL or F_p-DL): P(alpha < 1/3) = 0.1%.

Single best next experiment: Test LP_exc^rel directly where C's single-profile envelope corollary stops — on 64-to-112-bit split N at (n, m) in {(8,3), (10,4), (12,4)} over Q(sqrt(2)), use lattice enumeration in distinct conjugate-weighting cones (rather than exhaustive {-1,0,1}^r) inside larger boxes E > 1 to target multi-profile archimedean cancellation |F(a)| <= X_0 = 3^D * N^(1/d), measuring whether proper-submodule-independent rank stays 0 as in C's 84/96-bit ternary runs.
